title: No update/upsert path — re-adding an existing id croaks on UNIQUE
updated: 2026-10-25T05:43:54Z
---

meta_${name}.id is UNIQUE, so calling add() twice with the same id dies with "Failed to add vector: UNIQUE constraint failed". There is no update() or upsert option to replace a stored vector/metadata. Add an explicit update (or add(..., replace => 1)) that rewrites both the vec_ and meta_ rows in one transaction, with a regression test.

2026-10-25 05:41 Done b4e66fc. Decision: add(..., replace => 1) rather than a separate update(); it overwrites vector, metadata and content as a whole (omitted fields are dropped), unknown id just adds. Test t/18_replace.t red against old lib (UNIQUE croak).
